Found a serious layout bug on 320px small phone: menu action buttons overflow horizontally — "GARAGE" button is cut off at right edge (visible circle "..." partially, likely mute button offscreen). The button row `menu-actions` uses flex and Play 130 + Garage 124 + mute 52 + gaps => > 276 width. The mute round button is offscreen. Also tag/title fit. This fails responsive on 320 width (iPhone SE 1st gen / small Android). Need fix.

Also on 320, the menu title "RIDE THE RIDGELINE" wraps into 2 lines and overlaps the brand row/car? Actually brand row "RIDGE RUSH 3D" at y~230; title starts 280. The car behind is at y~190-280, causing brand row over car, but visually fine. The menu content extends to 544, within 568.

But the action row overflow is a bug. Fix CSS: allow wrapping or scale buttons on very small widths. Options:
- At max-width: 360px, reduce `.btn` padding and font-size, and `.menu-actions` flex-wrap? Wrapping would put mute on next line awkward.
- Make mute absolutely positioned relative to menu content? Better: hide the menu mute round button on very small widths? No, mute is useful, but there's also HUD mute during play. Menu mute could be positioned top-right instead of in action row. Currently menu-mute sits to the right of garage in `.menu-actions`. At 320, total widths: 130+124+52 + gaps 9*2 = 324 > 276, plus btn padding? `.btn-primary min-width 130`, garage width 124, btn-round 52 → 130+124+52+18=324. Need width 276. Reduce primary min-width to 112, padding 18, garage content ~103, mute 44 → 112+103+44+16=275. Fits exactly. Could implement at max-width 380px:
```
.menu-actions { gap: 8px; }
.btn { padding: 0 16px; font-size: 15px; }
.btn-primary { min-width: 112px; }
.btn-round { width: 44px; height: 44px; }
